.TH RMDIR "1" "July 2026" "PiggyOS" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
rmdir \- remove empty directories

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rmdir
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,DIRECTORY\/\fR...

.SH DESCRIPTION

.PP
Remove the DIRECTORY(ies), if they are empty.

.PP
Why are you not just using \fBrm\fP(1)?

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-p
remove DIRECTORY and its parents

.TP
.B \-v
output a message for every directory

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrm\fR(1)

